%erg v1
Title: Fix nextID to scan closed/ and archive/ subdirectories
Created: 2026-05-05
Author: haduong

--- log ---
2026-05-05T00:00Z haduong created

--- body ---
`tickets/tools/go/nextid.go` implements `nextID(dir string) string` which
scans `dir` for `NNNN-*.erg` filenames to determine the next sequential ID.
It only scans the top-level directory and ignores `dir/closed/` and
`dir/archive/` subdirectories.

When all active tickets have been closed and moved into `closed/`, the
top-level is empty and `nextID` restarts from `0001`, reusing IDs that
already exist in the archive. This happened in practice: tickets 0001–0011
were assigned IDs already present in `tickets/closed/` (0003–0012).

**Fix:** Walk all subdirectories of `dir` (or at minimum `closed/` and
`archive/`) when computing the maximum existing ID. The simplest approach:

```go
func nextID(dir string) string {
    max := 0
    _ = filepath.WalkDir(dir, func(path string, d fs.DirEntry, err error) error {
        if err != nil || d.IsDir() {
            return nil
        }
        if n := parseIDFromFilename(filepath.Base(path)); n > max {
            max = n
        }
        return nil
    })
    return fmt.Sprintf("%04d", max+1)
}
```

Extract `parseIDFromFilename` as a helper (integer parse of the leading
4-digit prefix, return 0 on non-match) so it can be unit-tested separately.

**Update `TestNextID` (ticket 0066):** add cases for
tickets in `closed/` and `archive/` subdirectories being respected by the
max-ID scan.
